    description: "## What\n\n27 open GitHub Dependabot alerts, **all in a single lockfile**: `packages/htrac-frontend/package-lock.json` (npm ecosystem). Surfaced 2026-07-26 during the post-cutover PERMANENT-checklist audit (item #9) — now that GitHub is origin, Dependabot is active and reporting.\n\nSeverity: **4 high / 17 medium / 6 low.** By package (alert counts):\n- `vite` — 8 alerts (dev/build tooling; dev-server-exposure class CVEs)\n- `dompurify` — 13 alerts (runtime XSS sanitizer — the one genuinely runtime-relevant dep)\n- `postcss` — 2, `brace-expansion` — 2, `esbuild` — 1, `file-type` — 1\n\n## Why this is LOW priority (not a migration issue, does not gate GitHub-PERMANENT)\n\n`htrac-frontend` is `\"private\": true`, v0.1.0 — a BlockSuite/Lit web frontend for `htrac serve` (ADR-0019). Consequences:\n- **Never published to npm** → no downstream consumer installs it.\n- **Not wired into any CI** — zero refs in `.woodpecker/` or `.github/`. The vulnerable build tooling (vite/esbuild/postcss) is never even run in the pipeline.\n- **Zero overlap with the shipped Python wheels** — hypergumbo/htrac ship as Python; end users are not exposed to these npm deps.\n- Real exposure is limited to whoever runs the local `htrac serve` bundled UI. Only `dompurify` is runtime-relevant (matters if that UI renders untrusted HTML — for a local tool serving your own tracker data, low practical risk).\n\nPre-existing frontend hygiene, not migration-caused. Not soak-relevant.\n\n## Fix (contained, npm-only, touches zero Python)\n\n26 of 27 alerts list a patched version → an `npm audit fix` / targeted dep bump in `packages/htrac-frontend/`, committing the updated `package-lock.json`, clears them in one contained PR.\n\n- **Lone holdout:** alert **#20** (`dompurify`, low severity) is `no-fix` (no patched release) → leave, or dismiss-with-note in the Dependabot UI.\n- **Caveat / why it's not a blind auto-fix:** the bump needs a node toolchain + a local `npm run build` / `vite preview` to confirm it survives the pinned `@blocksuite/* 0.17.33` / `vite 6` constraints. Because the package is **not in CI**, there is no automated regression net — a broken bump won't be caught by the pipeline. Verify the frontend still builds before merging.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `packages/htrac-frontend/package-lock.json` bumped so `gh api \".../dependabot/alerts?state=open\"` returns only the known `no-fix` holdout (alert #20) — or 0 if that one is dismissed.\n- `npm run build` in `packages/htrac-frontend/` succeeds against the bumped deps (BlockSuite/vite pins intact).\n- No Python package touched."  # 77a0
    fields: {}  # 77a0
